<p>The <em><a href="https://mathematicalphilosophy.org/mathphil" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Journal of Mathematical Philosophy</a> </em>is a new open-access journal.<span id="more-57971"></span></p>
<p><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" class="size-full wp-image-57981 aligncenter" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/journal-of-mathematical-philosophy.png" alt="" width="752" height="329" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/journal-of-mathematical-philosophy.png 752w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/journal-of-mathematical-philosophy-300x131.png 300w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/journal-of-mathematical-philosophy-400x175.png 400w" sizes="(max-width: 752px) 100vw, 752px" /></p>
<p>According to an announcement from its editors, the journal is &#8220;the first open access journal that is devoted to mathematical philosophy.&#8221;</p>
<p>It is now open to submissions in subject areas such as as formal epistemology, philosophical logic, philosophy of science, decision theory, philosophy of mathematics, formal metaphysics, philosophy of language, formal ethics, and philosophy of AI.</p>
<p>Published by LMU Munich, the <em>Journal of Mathematical Philosophy</em> is a &#8220;diamond&#8221; open-access journal, meaning that there are no author fees nor reader fees. The journal will make use of double-anonymous reviewing.</p>
<p>The journal is led by co-editors-in-chief <a href="https://jlandes.wordpress.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Jürgen Landes</a> and <a href="https://lennart.phd/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lennart Ackermans</a>, both of LMU Munich.</p>
<p>The inaugural associate editors are Francesca Zaffora Blando, Thomas Boyer-Kassem, Justin Bruner, Lorenzo Casini, Gustavo Cevolani, Kenny Easwaran, Ben Eva, Branden Fitelson, Sam Fletcher, Alexander Gebharter, Conrad Heilmann, Bennet Holman, Ekaterina Kubyshkina, Stephan Leuenberger, Conor Mayo-Wilson, Mattia Petrolo, Giuseppe Primero, Saeed Salehi, Jonah Schupbach, Dunja Šešelja, Ted Shear, Eric Snyder, Reuben Stern, Rush Stewart, Christian Strasser, David Teira, Brout Trpin, Olav Vassend, and Sylvia Wenmakers. The inaugural advisory board consists of Michael Glanzberg, Stephan Hartmann, Jan-Willem Romeijn, Jacob Stegenga, and Edward Zalta.</p>
<p>You can learn more about the journal at <a href="https://mathematicalphilosophy.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">its website</a>.</p><p>The post <a href="https://dailynous.com/2026/08/03/new-journal-of-mathematical-philosophy/">New: Journal of Mathematical Philosophy</a> first appeared on <a href="https://dailynous.com">Daily Nous</a>.</p>